Based on the simulated returns of the synthetic pieces individually, I can calculate an expected return for our TSM counterpart using the equation <br>
<center> $\mathbb{E} [R_B | R_A=r] = \mu_B + \rho \frac{\sigma_B}{\sigma_A} (r-\mu_A) $  </center> <br>
where $R_B$ is our TSM return per individual return $R_A$ for each synthetic piece. The total projected portfolio return will be the summation.

